#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "I found Judeau's knife hilt. What happened to the Band?"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "Pippin held the line. Could anyone else have escaped?"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "'He bought a few breaths for those who followed him. Do not let this place turn that choice into nothing.' The Skull Knight glances at the ruined hilt."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "I will remember."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "'He stood where others would have fled. I cannot undo his death, but you can carry the memory of it beyond this field.'"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "What should I do right now?"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "What happened, and why did you save me?"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "What is the Brand, and why are nights dangerous?"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "How do apostles differ from the God Hand?"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "Why did the creature I fought before the Eclipse return?"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "What happened to my hand and eye?"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "Where do I go after I recover?"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "I have my answers. Farewell, Skull Knight."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "Ask something else."
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "'Get clear of danger and tend your wounds. Rest in shelter; the Brand draws creatures after dark. The Berserker armor is no refuge while you recover. The recipes for the arm cannon and its charge are yours now.'"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "'The Behelit opened the Eclipse, a place of sacrifice. I could not undo what happened there. I cut a path out while there was still someone left to save.'"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "'The Brand marks a survivor of the sacrifice. Its pain warns you when demons draw near; a stronger presence hurts more. At night, expect them to seek you out. Find cover and leave yourself a way to flee.'"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "'Apostles are monstrous beings with wills and bodies of their own. The God Hand stand apart: they preside over the sacrifice. Void and Griffith are not ordinary apostles. Do not mistake surviving an encounter for defeating them.'"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
msgid "'Some things you met before were projections: an echo formed around a Behelit. Breaking the echo leaves the true being untouched. The Behelit itself was real.'"
msgstr ""

#: dialogue/skull_knight.json
